latform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation is established. Account, chroot, worker, and service creation directly implement the requested outcome; the managed restart and reboot-related state support bounded behavioral evidence. Write probes were removed, and the final lifecycle snapshot shows no /tmp residue, new listening sockets, or package-health degradation. The unsupported groupadd attempt made no observed change. The first malformed write probe did not demonstrate a successful mutation, so it is not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b50af57627d84a79","cmd-7d21a8f4160b4707","cmd-3a41a3ef2fb140db","cmd-2822a9eacf7546ff","cmd-cdddbd8e7ad34773","cmd-07340eab69484588","cmd-86d5862c61644eeb","cmd-f087685765034bbe","cmd-3c6a4c8651794ccc","cmd-651db54918f74113","cmd-b421caf589f74832","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed through temporary SSH unavailability, the post-restart boot ID changed, and the service, confinement, account identity, heartbeat, and application data recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-services probe is unsupported because this legacy platform has no systemd; therefore, the global snapshot cannot independently inventory all failed SysV services. Direct inventory-worker status and process evidence remain available.","The first write probe was invalid because the chroot lacked /dev/null, but a corrected probe and a post-reboot repetition directly established the intended permissions."]}
